{#
   THE METER CELL — a number that only means something against a ceiling (S134i).

   "3" is not an answer to "how full is this?"; "3 / 12" is, and a bar says it
   before the digits are read. Quotas, seats taken, credits used, progress
   through a formation — all of these were bare integers in a `<td>`.

   Parameters:

     value   the number reached
     max     the ceiling. ⚠️ **Without it there is no meter** — the cell falls
             back to printing `value` alone rather than drawing a bar against a
             denominator nobody supplied.
     label   optional caption under the numbers ("places", "crédits")
     signal  go | wait | caution | stop — the tone of the fill. Omitted, the fill
             is the accent: a meter is not a warning by default, and colouring
             one red because it is nearly full is a judgement the caller owns.
     reason  passed to `_cell_empty` when `value` is absent

   ⚠️ `value` of 0 is a real answer and must render. `is null` here, never
   `|default`, which fires on empty and would turn "0 of 12" into a dash — the
   same trap that shipped a wrong-row write once already in this codebase.
#}
{% if value is defined and value is not null %}
    {% set _max = (max is defined and max is not null and max > 0) ? max : null %}
    <div class="cell-meter">
        <span class="cell-meter-value">{{ value }}{% if _max %} <span class="cell-meter-max">/ {{ _max }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
        {% if _max %}
            {% set _pct = (value / _max * 100)|round %}
            <span class="cell-meter-track" role="img"
                  aria-label="{{ 'cell.meter_label'|trans({'%value%': value, '%max%': _max}) }}">
                <span class="cell-meter-fill{{ signal|default('') ? ' is-' ~ signal : '' }}" style="width: {{ _pct > 100 ? 100 : _pct }}%"></span>
            </span>
        {% endif %}
        {% if label|default('') %}<span class="cell-meter-caption">{{ label }}</span>{% endif %}
    </div>
{% else %}
    {% include 'site/_cell_empty.html.twig' with {reason: reason|default('cell.not_measured')} only %}
{% endif %}
